 +4\epsilon^4 \nonumber\\
 &=4\epsilon-6\epsilon^2+10\epsilon^3+O(\epsilon^4).
 \label{eq:s-three-energy}
\end{align}

To compute the relative entropy up to order $\epsilon^3$, we need the first six powers of $\delta_\epsilon$, since its leading term is of order $\sqrt\epsilon$.
Expanding the ratio in Eq.~\eqref{eq:s-three-wigner-ratio} gives
