 +O\!\left(\epsilon^{7/2}(1+R^2)\right).
 \label{eq:s-three-deviation-expansion}
\end{align}
The constant in the remainder bound is independent of $x$ and $p$.
We justify the integration of this expansion before evaluating its coefficients.
Because $\delta_\epsilon$ is a polynomial of degree at most four in $x,p$ with coefficients $O(\sqrt\epsilon)$, we have
